{
  "_comment": [
    "Frame data per weapon class. Times are in seconds; the simulation runs at a",
    "fixed 60Hz so these convert to whole frames.",
    "  windup   - the tell. Longer means the attack is readable and punishable.",
    "  active   - how long the hitbox is live.",
    "  recovery - the commitment. This is where a Souls game is won or lost.",
    "  damage   - motion value, multiplied into the weapon's base damage.",
    "  poise    - stagger damage dealt.",
    "  step     - metres the attacker slides forward, giving swings their weight.",
    "  arc      - degrees the hitbox sweeps through; a thrust is narrow, a",
    "             greataxe swing is nearly a full circle.",
    "Weapons inherit the moveset for their class and can override any field."
  ],

